d therapy</article-title><source><italic>Annals of the Rheumatic Diseases</italic></source><year>2011</year><volume>70</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>i37</fpage><lpage>i43</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">21339217</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B19"><label>10</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ramos</surname><given-names>PS</given-names></name><name><surname>Williams</surname><given-names>AH</given-names></name><name><surname>Ziegler</surname><given-names>JT</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Genetic analyses of interferon pathway-related genes reveal multiple new loci associated with systemic lupus erythematosus</article-title><source><italic>Arthritis and Rheumatism</italic></source><year>2011</year><volume>63</volume><issue>7</issue><fpage>2049</fpage><lpage>2057</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">21437871</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B14"><label>11</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kammer</surname><given-names>GM</given-names></name><name><surname>Perl</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Richardson</surname><given-names>BC</given-names></name><name><surname>Tsokos</surname><given-names>GC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Review: abnormal T cell signal transduction in systemic lupus erythematosus</article-title><source><italic>Arthritis and Rheumatism</italic></source><year>2002</year><volume>46</volume><issue>5</issue><fpage>1139</fpage><lpage>1154</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12115215</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B15"><label>12</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Shah</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>WW</given-names></name><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>SH</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Dysregulated balance of Th17 and Th1 cells in systemic lupus erythematosus</article-title><source><italic>Arthritis Research and Therapy</italic></source><year>2010</year><volume>12</volume><issue>2, article no. R53</issue></element-citation></ref><ref id="B16"><label>13</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tsokos</surname><given-names>GC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Systemic lupus erythematosus</article-title><source><italic>New England Journal of Medicine</italic></source><year>2011</year><volume>365</volume><issue>22</issue><fpage>2110</fpage><lpage>2121</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">22129255</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B8"><label>14</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gaipl</surname><given-names>US</given-names></name><name><surname>Munoz</surname><given-names>LE</given-names></name><name><surname>Grossmayer</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Clearance deficiency and systemic lupus erythematosus (SLE)</article-title><source><italic>Journal of Autoimmunity</italic></source><year>2007</year><volume>28</volume><issue>2-3</issue><fpage>114</fpage><lpage>121</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17368845</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B9"><label>15</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Munoz</surname><given-names>LE</given-names></name><name><surname>Gaipl</surname><given-names>US</given-names></name><name><surname>Franz</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>SLE&#x02014;a disease of clearance deficiency?</article-title><source><italic>Rheumatology</italic></source><year>2005</year><volume>44</volume><issue>9</issue><fpage>1101</fpage><lpage>1107</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15928001</pub-id>